353
00:18:14,000 --> 00:18:15,000
to the IBM crowd.

354
00:18:15,000 --> 00:18:18,000
And there's a crowd of brokers there who are trading.

355
00:18:18,000 --> 00:18:20,000
And you just do it.

356
00:18:20,000 --> 00:18:26,000
Verbally, you talk to them and you make a trade.

357
00:18:26,000 --> 00:18:27,000
That's really old-fashioned.

358
00:18:27,000 --> 00:18:29,500
There is something more electronic and modern

359
00:18:29,500 --> 00:18:32,000
about the New York Stock Exchange, but that

360
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:36,000
specialist post behavior still persists.

361
00:18:36,000 --> 00:18:37,000
Most of the world is switching over.

362
00:18:37,000 --> 00:18:40,000
Most of the world is switching over to electronic trading.

363
00:18:40,000 --> 00:18:43,500
And so, things happen that – so, for

364
00:18:43,500 --> 00:18:47,000
example, in India, they developed another stock exchange

